It looks like this can broke some other cases, e.g.:

```lua
local dialog = Dialog("Canvas Resize Test")
dialog
:canvas{
    width = 200,
    height = 200,
    onpaint = function(ev)
      local context = ev.context
        dialog 
        :modify{id = "canvas-width", text = tostring(context.width)} 
        :modify{id = "canvas-height", text = tostring(context.height)}
    end
}
:label{id = "canvas-width", label = "Width:"}
:label{id = "canvas-height", label = "Height:"}
:button{id = "resize", text = "Resize", onclick=function()
	  local rc = dialog.bounds
	  rc.width = rc.width + 10
	  dialog.bounds = rc
       end}
dialog:show{wait = false}
```

The new "Resize" button works in the current version making the window bigger, but not with this fix.

